      "label": "library-new-request",
      "body": "### Reason for requesting the library\n\nA Spring Boot native application using `micrometer-registry-otlp` builds\nsuccessfully but fails at runtime while creating `OtlpMeterRegistry`.\n\n## Environment\n\n- Spring Boot: 4.1.0\n- GraalVM Native Build Tools Gradle plugin: 1.1.7\n- Oracle GraalVM: 25.0.4\n- Java: 25\n- io.micrometer:micrometer-registry-otlp:1.17.0\n- io.opentelemetry.proto:opentelemetry-proto:1.10.0-alpha\n- com.google.protobuf:protobuf-java:4.34.2\n- Native image built with Spring Boot/Paketo `bootBuildImage`\n\n## Regression\n\nThe deployment workflow and application dependencies were unchanged.\n\nThe only change was upgrading:\n\n```diff\n- id(\"org.graalvm.buildtools.native\") version \"0.11.5\"\n+ id(\"org.graalvm.buildtools.native\") version \"1.1.7\"\n```\n\nWith 0.11.5, the native application starts successfully.\nWith 1.1.7, the image builds successfully but fails during startup.\n\nThe exact change is available here:\n\nhttps://github.com/mingchiuli/megalith-micro/commit/ff8f3c6f\n\n## Failure\n\n```text\nCaused by: org.graalvm.nativeimage.MissingReflectionRegistrationError:\nCannot reflectively invoke method\n'public static com.google.protobuf.ExtensionRegistry\ncom.google.protobuf.ExtensionRegistry.getEmptyRegistry()'\n\nat java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke(Method.java:562)\nat com.google.protobuf.ExtensionRegistryFactory.invokeSubclassFactory(ExtensionRegistryFactory.java:63)\nat com.google.protobuf.ExtensionRegistryFactory.createEmpty(ExtensionRegistryFactory.java:45)\nat com.google.protobuf.ExtensionRegistryLite.getEmptyRegistry(ExtensionRegistryLite.java:107)\nat com.google.protobuf.AbstractParser.<clinit>(AbstractParser.java:52)\nat com.google.protobuf.UnknownFieldSet.<clinit>(UnknownFieldSet.java:1119)\nat io.opentelemetry.proto.resource.v1.Resource.<clinit>(Resource.java:1480)\nat io.micrometer.registry.otlp.OtlpMeterRegistry.<init>(OtlpMeterRegistry.java:129)\n```\n\n## Verified workaround\n\nAdding the following reflection metadata and rebuilding makes the native\napplication start successfully:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"reflection\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"com.google.protobuf.ExtensionRegistry\",\n      \"methods\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"getEmptyRegistry\",\n          \"parameterTypes\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe equivalent Spring `RuntimeHints` registration was also verified with\n`nativeCompile` on Oracle GraalVM 25.0.4.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`micrometer-registry-otlp` should initialize in a native image without\nrequiring application-specific reflection hints.\n\n## Related issue\n\nThe same missing reflection registration was previously reported for\n`grpc-xds` in #6307 and addressed by #7199. That metadata is scoped to\n`grpc-xds`, so it does not cover the Micrometer OTLP code path.",
      "body_error": ""
